1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,461
The first report that Jesus was risen was dismissed

2
00:00:02,521 --> 00:00:05,221
as nonsense by His own apostles.

3
00:00:05,741 --> 00:00:07,982
And their words seemed to them as idle tales,

4
00:00:08,542 --> 00:00:09,682
and they believed them not.

5
00:00:09,862 --> 00:00:12,583
The report came from women and in that world,

6
00:00:12,863 --> 00:00:14,863
a woman's word carried almost no weight in

7
00:00:14,923 --> 00:00:15,223
court.

8
00:00:16,164 --> 00:00:17,904
No one inventing a resurrection would open

9
00:00:17,924 --> 00:00:18,304
it there.

10
00:00:19,234 --> 00:00:20,174
They watched Him die.

11
00:00:21,114 --> 00:00:22,415
They saw where He was buried.

12
00:00:23,495 --> 00:00:24,875
At dawn, they were back.

13
00:00:26,015 --> 00:00:28,316
So the angels pointed them to His own promise:

14
00:00:28,876 --> 00:00:30,737
Why seek ye the living among the dead?

15
00:00:31,477 --> 00:00:34,357
He is not here, but is risen: remember how

16
00:00:34,397 --> 00:00:36,638
he spake unto you when he was yet in Galilee,

17
00:00:36,898 --> 00:00:39,299
Saying, The Son of man must be delivered into

18
00:00:39,339 --> 00:00:42,079
the hands of sinful men, and be crucified,

19
00:00:42,619 --> 00:00:44,200
and the third day rise again.

20
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,860
They had followed Him closely enough to hear

21
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:46,700
that promise made.

22
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:50,161
The idle tale was true, and it went first to

23
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:52,001
the witnesses the world would not hear.

24
00:00:53,222 --> 00:00:55,182
He still sends His word to the overlooked.

25
00:00:55,962 --> 00:00:58,563
Stop seeking the living among the dead the

26
00:00:58,603 --> 00:01:00,403
risen Christ is seeking you.
